  <h2>The bottom line</h2>
  <p>Firecrawl is a fine tool and a fair default for markdown-first work. The right alternative depends on what you need next to the markdown. If you want open-source control, Crawl4AI and ScrapeGraphAI lead. If you want a focused scraping API, ScrapingBee and ScraperAPI are clean choices. If you want clean markdown plus structured data, intelligence, vertical actors, and browser automation behind one key, one bill, and pay-as-you-go pricing that refunds failed calls, that is the gap Ollagraph was built to fill.</p>

  <p>The honest way to decide is to run your own URLs through two or three options and compare the output on the sites you actually depend on. Ollagraph gives you 1,000 free credits to do exactly that — no card, every endpoint. Browse the <a href="/capabilities">capabilities</a>, read the <a href="/docs">docs</a>, or compare pricing on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> when you are ready.</p>
